% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `monogyny_list_index`, compiled
% by psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: no part of
% it is printed.  Step 3n (docs/simpos/boot_route.md §6).
% Its source is INTERPOLATED (labelled) from:
%   - pimfep##simpos_user (held .ptf, cells read 2026-11-25 with
%     psi/fepread/ptfread.py): local users/3 (@11c-12b) makes the class
%     slot `users` with `:create(#monogyny_list_index, U)` on first use;
%     regist/4 (@4d-61) sends `:put_at(Users, User, Name)` after making
%     the user, identify/4 (@66-72) `:get_at(Users, User, Name)`, and
%     setup_process/4 (@7f-9e) tries identify/4 first and regist/4 when it
%     fails: so get_at/3 fails on a name never put, and put_at/3 adds one;
%   - the selectors held programs send (docs/simpos/required/classes.tsv
%     row monogyny_list_index: create/2 and add_at/3, clear/1, get_at/3,
%     get_contents/2, get_contents_with_key/2, get_keys/2, put_at/3,
%     put_contents/2, put_contents_with_key/2, remove_at/3, stick_tap/2),
%     the list_index protocol plus put_at/3.
% INFERENCE: it is a list_index (nature list_index: the same selectors)
% that holds ONE object per key ("monogyny"): put_at/3 replaces what the
% key held.  Only put_at/3 is new here; the rest, create/2 included, is
% the list_index stand-in's.

class monogyny_list_index has
nature list_index;

% create/2 is list_index's (inherited: users/3 above sends
% `:create(#monogyny_list_index, U)`).  A create/2 here as well is
% combined with the inherited one (the Librarian's inheritance; measured
% 2026-11-25: two solutions, two indexes).

instance

% INTERPOLATED from: regist/4 above (Object before Key, as add_at/3).
% INFERENCE: the key's old object, if any, is removed first.
:put_at(Index, Object, Key) :-
        remove_old(Index, Key),
        :add_at(Index, Object, Key);

local
remove_old(Index, Key) :- :remove_at(Index, _, Key), !;
remove_old(_, _);
end.
